You can add children to router links (vue/router/index.js)
the children do not get a slash in the path because they automatically get a slash when clicked
<router-link to="/{path}" > is the equivalent to an a element in HTML in Vue
you can also do a router link to a child path in a nav bar for example (with <router-link to="/{path}/{childpath}">)

    {
      path: '/',
      name: 'home',
      component: HomeView,
      children: ({
            path: '',
            name: "overview",
            component: defaultOverviewView,
      })
    },

    Then you can add additional router links and router paths and such like normal


    the highest routes need a slash in order to define, but any children do not require slashes

